BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rutland County Candidate Forum
DTSTART:20261005T180000
DTEND:20261005T193000
DTSTAMP:20261005T194949Z
UID:a9f602fca8a5eec964e2a5f1493bac@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:There will be a candidate forum on 10/5/26 from 6-7:30\, held 
 at Godnick Adult Center\, 1 Deer Street\, Rutland. We're looking forward t
 o a thoughtful conversation about early childhood and family issues in our
  community. The event is facilitated by the Rutland Building Bright Future
 s Early Childhood Council. Building Bright Futures is Vermont's Early Chil
 dhood State Advisory Council network\, the entity responsible for advising
  the Governor and Legislature on the well-being of young children (prenata
 l to age eight) and their families. Regional Councils convene community me
 mbers and partners serving young children and families to identify communi
 ty needs and create opportunities to strengthen both local and statewide s
 ystems of care\, health\, and education. Each candidate will have 2 minute
 s to respond to each question. Responses should be directed to the moderat
 or\, Stephanie Carvey — this is not a debate format\, so there will be n
 o direct exchanges or rebuttals between candidates. As time allows\, we wi
 ll also incorporate a small number of questions submitted by attendees at 
 check-in. All candidates who won their primaries have been invited to this
  event. For any questions\, please contact Darla Senecal at dsenecal@build
 ingbrightfutures.org.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Godnick Adult Center\, 1 Deer Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/rutland-co
 unty-candidate-forum-01-10-2026-15-06-27
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shakespeare Out Loud
DTSTART:20261005T160000
DTEND:20261005T173000
DTSTAMP:20261005T194949Z
UID:2d44fda1d388592cc7ba15cb4819d5@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Gathering of interested adults to read aloud Shakespeare’s p
 lays. This Current Play: The Most Lamentable Tragedy of Romeo and Juliet b
 y William Shakespeare. No experience or expertise required\; we will gathe
 r\, select parts and read this engaging play aloud. Bring a text from whic
 h to read. All are welcome to come and read or sit and listen as the play 
 unfolds. Every week through Oct 05\, 2026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/shakespear
 e-out-loud-16-09-2026-00-19-32
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with David Sedaris
DTSTART:20261006T193000
DTEND:20261006T213000
DTSTAMP:20261005T194949Z
UID:f660b911e0c2fe28b2c0706a9f673a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Our friends and downtown neighbors at Phoenix Books will be on
 -site with a wide variety of David’s publications available for purchase
 . With sardonic wit and incisive social observation\, David Sedaris has be
 come one of America’s preeminent humor writers. Beloved for his personal
  essays and short stories\, Sedaris is the bestselling author of Barrel Fe
 ver\, Holidays on Ice\, Naked\, Me Talk Pretty One Day\, Dress Your Family
  in Corduroy and Denim\, When You Are Engulfed in Flames\, Let’s Explore
  Diabetes with Owls\, Calypso\, The Best of Me and Happy-Go-Lucky\, among 
 others. His books have sold more than 16 million copies worldwide and been
  translated into 32 languages. 30 Center St Rutland \, Vermont 05701 802-7
 75-0903 boxoffice@paramountvt.org https://www.paramountvt.org/ Submit An E
